                                   Autoscaling

--> Autoscaling is a service that automatically increase or decreses the number of ec2 instance
   based on the application workload or demand

--> it automatically adjust the capacity based on demand.

--> types of Autoscaling:
1. Horizontal scaling
--> Horizontal scaling means adding or removing EC2 instances.
--> Instead of making one server bigger, we create more servers.

2. Vertical Scaling
--> Vertical scaling means increasing or decreasing the size/capacity of an existing EC2 instance.
--> Instead of adding more servers, we make the existing server more powerful.


